{"at": "2026-11-05T15:12:44.582001+00:00", "event_id": "01M6P49Z16Q9SZ6CWPA2KRE91H", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M6P49YZNEAW11TA5ZH6WMD23", "input_key": "budget_approach", "mission_id": "01M6P49EBJZ15Q06S9XYQE61HX", "mission_slug": "corpus-advisory-budget-01M6P49E", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["derive cap + legible expiry", "path shard"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "Acceptance is p95 <= 75% of timeout-minutes over a week of main and PR runs. Measurement: p95 20.3 min (102% of the 20-min cap), with ~11.5 min of the ~19.5 min run spent on fixed costs (whole-tree pytest collection, serial wall-clock policy scan) that two pinned guards forbid narrowing. Confirm the approach: derive the cap from the measured max with the repo's #5378 formula and make a budget expiry legible as INCOMPLETE (#4437), documenting why sharding is ruled out -- or shard the corpus selection by path and edit the two pinned guards?", "recorded_at": "2026-11-05T15:12:44.582001Z", "run_id": "01M6P49YZNEAW11TA5ZH6WMD23", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-05T15:12:44.533815Z", "step_id": "specify.budget.approach"}}
{"at": "2026-11-05T15:12:47.783759+00:00", "event_id": "01M6P4A257YSVGMM21HRPFQXXX", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M6P49YZNEAW11TA5ZH6WMD23", "final_answer": "Derive the cap from measurement. Operator guidance (batch-11 D1 brief): measure first, do not just raise the number; a cancellation must not read as a failure. Measured: p95 20.3 min = 102% of the 20-min cap; fixed costs (whole-tree collection ~8 min, serial wall-clock policy scan ~3.5 min on PRs) are architectural -- tests/ci/test_corpus_blocking_home.py requires tree-wide corpus reach and tests/ci/test_contracts_routing.py requires exactly one pytest invocation, so a path shard would weaken the lane. Fix: record the measured max suite in the repo's #5378 headroom form, derive the cap with ceil((max+0:30)*1.5) = 31, extend the cap guard to enforce it for this job, and make a budget expiry read as INCOMPLETE-advisory rather than a failed test (#4437). Selection semantics, deselects, continue-on-error and trigger stay unchanged.", "mission_id": "01M6P49EBJZ15Q06S9XYQE61HX", "mission_slug": "corpus-advisory-budget-01M6P49E", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-11-05T15:12:47.783759Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M6P49YZNEAW11TA5ZH6WMD23", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-05T15:12:47.782850Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
